  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_307_4a_o2` (8 witnesses), and `task_result.md` is written in the working directory.\n\n**Budget mistake:** I used 4 of the 6 gate runs, and two were wasted. The first ran on the untouched skeleton, which I already knew would fail. The second was my error: I ran the gate command with `| head -0` appended, which broke the \"run exactly this command\" rule and discarded the output. The files were still the skeleton at that point, so nothing was lost beyond the run. Both are recorded in `task_result.md`. The third run failed to build (`Term.measure` takes two arguments, not three) and the fourth passed.\n\n**Rule** (`NRS_484B_307_4a_o2.lean`):\n- **Applicability:** the subject (both traffic and a vehicle) faces a traffic signal showing a green turn arrow (left, right or u_turn) and none of the other 22 indications. \"Facing\" means the subject is on an approach lane that the signal governs and that enters the intersection. It also covers a subject that is now in the intersection, provided it has stayed there since it was last on that lane.\n- **Obligation:** the same intersection, lane and signal are selected again, and the duty applies at every such selection. For every other road user who is either a pedestrian in a crosswalk marking an entrance to that intersection, or any traffic inside the intersection, the subject must not move faster than `p.halt_speed_tolerance` while either:\n  - a crash is in danger: the centres come within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` inside `p.conflict_horizon`; or\n  - the two bodies are in contact.\n- **Narrowings:** none of my own. The only open choices were the record's own reading of \"lawfully\" and \"the adjacent crosswalk\", written as the record states them.\n\n**Witnesses:** the five planned scenes (`forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind`, `branch_1`), plus three I added:\n- **`branch_2`** (violated): the subject collides with another vehicle moving at the same velocity. Only the contact part of the rule catches this.\n- **`branch_3`** (violated): the subject is still in its own lane, heading at a pedestrian in the crosswalk at that lane's entrance.\n- **`branch_4`** (not applicable): the green left arrow shows together with a circular red, so it is not \"alone\".\n\nNothing in the node needed reporting as a defect.",
